        "original_id": "9c2c7fc8-b1dc-567e-ba0e-e4da5e7e6eaf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Rescuers, The Muppets\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Buena Vista Distribution\n- People: Jeanette Nolan\n- Topics: animated films, musical comedy films, television roles, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- Jeanette Nolan appeared in the television series \"The Virginian\" from 1962 to 1971.\n- Jeanette Nolan appeared in the film \"Macbeth\" in 1948.\n- Jeanette Nolan appeared in the television series \"Dirty Sally\" in 1974.\n- Walt Disney Productions produced \"The Rescuers,\" a 1977 American animated comedy-drama adventure film.\n- Buena Vista Distribution first released \"The Rescuers\" on June 22, 1977.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Ellie Mae in the Disney animated film \"The Rescuers\" in 1977.\n- Jeanette Nolan voiced Widow Tweed in the Disney animated film \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.\n- \"The Muppets\" is a 2011 American musical comedy film.\n- \"The Muppets\" was the seventh theatrical film featuring the Muppets.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c5a49a62-2ed7-502f-b513-1bcd090c531b",
        "text": "Page: The Rescuers. Sentence: The Rescuers is a 1977 American animated comedy-drama adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions and first released on June 22, 1977, by Buena Vista Distribution.\nPage: The Muppets (film). Sentence: The Muppets is a 2011 American musical comedy film and the seventh theatrical film featuring the Muppets.\nPage: Jeanette Nolan. Sentence: She is best known for her roles in the television series \"The Virginian\" (1962 - 1971) and \"Dirty Sally\" (1974); and in films such as \"Macbeth\" (1948) and as the voices of Ellie Mae and Widow Tweed in the animated Disney films, \"The Rescuers\" (1977) and \"The Fox and the Hound\" (1981) respectively.",
